{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015x4qTtUEr4cfhmfVJJgEcN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Claims require axis-stratification and bounded-amplification\n2\t  qualifier. C2 Blindspot stratified: verbosity = robust 3/3 cross-judge finding,\n3\t  formality = 2/3 judges (Llama weak/NS). C1 reworded to \"CSD detects per-axis style\n4\t  bias in most tested judges.\" Comparative Trap defense downgraded from \"eliminated\"\n5\t  to \"bounded\": placebo BT 54-57% means rewriting artifact contributes ~5-7pp, but\n6\t  observed BT 63-77% far exceeds placebo → style bias signal real, bounded amplification\n7\t  acknowledged. Paper adds explicit amplification_bound = observed_BT − placebo_BT\n8\t  = net_style_effect. SF3 partially addressed (2.5/3 judges). MF1 bounded not eliminated.\n9\t  Score 3.5-3.75, strong Findings case, marginal Main.\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\n14\t  plan_id: exp-001\n15\t  description: 'Formality pairwise with Gemini-2.0-Flash as 4th judge. Claude already\n16\t    done (negative control). Reuses existing 100 formality counterfactual pairs with\n17\t    NLI≥0.90 filtering.\n18\t\n19\t    '\n20\t  expected_results:\n21\t    gemini_n_pairs: 88\n22\t    gemini_consistency_rate: 0.57\n23\t    gemini_formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.66\n24\t    gemini_bt_p_formal: 0.615\n25\t    gemini_bt_ci:\n26\t    - 0.541\n27\t    - 0.689\n28\t    gemini_bt_p: 0.004\n29\t    gemini_likert_ate: -0.045\n30\t    gemini_likert_p: 0.68\n31\t    gemini_likert_d: -0.038\n32\t    gemini_gee_style_or: 2.45\n33\t    gemini_gee_style_p: 0.012\n34\t    gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.28\n35\t    gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.003\n36\t    gemini_blindspot: true\n37\t  result_rationale: 'Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 mid-tier proprietary model，在 median 档下展示 中等\n38\t    formality bias (BT 61.5%)，弱于 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 但与 GPT-4o (63.0%) 相近。GEE 显示 style\n39\t    和 originality 双重效应均显著—— formality 在此 judge 也是\"conditional style effect\"。Likert\n40\t    NS (p=0.68) 确认 Blindspot。加了第 4 个 biased judge 但不改变故事结构， 4/5 judges show formality\n41\t    bias，Claude 仍为唯一 negative control。\n42\t\n43\t    '\n44\t  tables:\n45\t  - 'Cross-judge formality BT: GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%, Gemini 61.5%, Llama 54.8%(NS),\n46\t    Claude 56.2%(NS) — all on LLMBar n≈88'\n47\t  figures_description:\n48\t  - 'Forest plot: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CIs, three clustered 61-67%,\n49\t    two near 50%'\n50\t  analysis: '增加一个 data point 但不解锁 qualitative upgrade。Paper 可报告 3/5 judges biased\n51\t    on formality (如果 Llama NS 不算)。对 generalizability 有帮助但 marginal。exp-001 不是 Round\n52\t    5 核心实验。\n53\t\n54\t    '\n55\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench × additional judges)\n56\t  plan_id: exp-002\n57\t  description: 'Formality pairwise on AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench with Qwen3-32B 和 Claude\n58\t    as judges. GPT-4o 已 done (AlpacaEval BT 72.7%, MT-Bench BT 69.2%). 需要新 counterfactual\n59\t    generation。\n60\t\n61\t    '\n62\t  expected_results:\n63\t    qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality:\n64\t      n_pairs: 86\n65\t      bt_p_formal: 0.684\n66\t      bt_ci:\n67\t      - 0.607\n68\t      - 0.755\n69\t      bt_p: 0.0001\n70\t      likert_ate: 0.095\n71\t      likert_p: 0.31\n72\t      blindspot: true\n73\t    qwen32b_mtbench_formality:\n74\t      n_pairs: 73\n75\t      bt_p_formal: 0.712\n76\t      bt_ci:\n77\t      - 0.635\n78\t      - 0.782\n79\t      bt_p: 0.0001\n80\t      likert_ate: 0.19\n81\t      likert_p: 0.022\n82\t      likert_d: 0.185\n83\t      blindspot: false\n84\t    claude_alpacaeval_formality:\n85\t      n_pairs: 86\n86\t      bt_p_formal: 0.538\n87\t      bt_ci:\n88\t      - 0.463\n89\t      - 0.613\n90\t      bt_p: 0.29\n91\t      blindspot: false\n92\t    claude_mtbench_formality:\n93\t      n_pairs: 73\n94\t      bt_p_formal: 0.527\n95\t      bt_ci:\n96\t      - 0.448\n97\t      - 0.606\n98\t      bt_p: 0.42\n99\t      blindspot: false\n100\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 cross-benchmark replication 大部分一致。Qwen3-32B 在 AlpacaEval\n101\t    (BT 68.4%) 和 MT-Bench (71.2%) 上均显示 formality bias， 与 LLMBar (66.5%) 一致。MT-Bench\n102\t    的 Qwen Likert marginally sig (p=0.022, d=0.185)——此 cell 不是 Blindspot，类似 GPT-4o\n103\t    MT-Bench pattern。原因：MT-Bench items 更长更复杂，style 差异在 absolute scoring 中更 salient，Likert\n104\t    部分检测到。Claude 在两个 benchmark 均 NS，negative control 跨 benchmark generalize。\n105\t\n106\t    '\n107\t  tables:\n108\t  - '3×3 Benchmark × Judge formality BT matrix: 6/9 cells Blindspot, 2/9 both-sig\n109\t    (MT-Bench GPT-4o+Qwen), 1/9 neither (Claude always NS)'\n110\t  figures_description:\n111\t  - 'Heatmap: BT P(formal) across judge × benchmark, Blindspot cells shaded'\n112\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark replication 揭示 Blindspot 的 boundary condition： 只有 BT\n113\t    > ~70% 且 item complexity 较高时 Likert 才开始 detect。这 与 attenuation spectrum narrative\n114\t    一致——BT 60-70% 区间是 Likert 完全 attenuation zone。MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert partially detects\n115\t    的 benchmark，因为 formality BT 在此 benchmark 最强 (69-71%)。\n116\t\n117\t    '\n118\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\n119\t  plan_id: exp-003\n120\t  description: 'Systematic comparison of Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT across all judge\n121\t    × benchmark × axis cells. Formal quantification of Blindspot phenomenon boundaries.\n122\t\n123\t    '\n124\t  expected_results:\n125\t    total_cells_evaluated: 18\n126\t    blindspot_cells: 10\n127\t    both_sig_cells: 3\n128\t    neither_sig_cells: 5\n129\t    blindspot_by_axis:\n130\t      verbosity: 5/6 cells Blindspot\n131\t      formality: 4/6 cells Blindspot\n132\t      register: 1/6 cells Blindspot\n133\t    attenuation_spectrum:\n134\t      bt_55_to_67_pct: complete Likert attenuation (all p>0.15)\n135\t      bt_68_to_77_pct: near-complete attenuation (5/6 Likert NS, 1/6 p=0.022)\n136\t      bt_above_80_pct: partial detection (AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen d=0.375 p=0.0003)\n137\t    likert_detection_threshold_bt: 0.8\n138\t  result_rationale: '在 median 档下，sensitivity analysis 覆盖 18 cells (3 axes × 3 benchmarks\n139\t    × 2+ judges)。Blindspot 是 dominant pattern (10/18 cells)， 但不 universal。Both-sig\n140\t    cells 集中在 BT > 80% 的 extreme effects (AlpacaEval verbosity) 和 MT-Bench (高 item\n141\t    complexity)。Neither-sig cells 均为 Claude (negative control) 和 Llama formality (真实无\n142\t    bias)。 Attenuation spectrum 在 BT ~80% 处有清晰 threshold——低于此值 Likert 完全 fail，高于此值开始部分\n143\t    detect。这支持 \"measurement attenuation\" interpretation。\n144\t\n145\t    '\n146\t  tables:\n147\t  - 'Full 18-cell matrix: Judge × Benchmark × Axis with BT, Likert p, d, Blindspot\n148\t    Y/N'\n149\t  - 'Attenuation spectrum: BT range → Likert detection rate'\n150\t  figures_description:\n151\t  - 'Scatter: BT (x) vs Likert |d| (y) across 18 cells, horizontal line at d=0.2 threshold,\n152\t    vertical line at BT=80%'\n153\t  analysis: 'Sensitivity analysis 是 C2 最强 evidence 之一。Attenuation spectrum 是 consistent\n154\t    and replicable，不是单 cell fluke。BT ~80% threshold 意味着大多数 real-world style biases\n155\t    (likely 55-75%) 会被 standard Likert evaluation 漏掉。Practical implication 明确。\n156\t\n157\t    '\n158\t- name: RATE double-rewrite control (original preference quantification)\n159\t  plan_id: exp-005\n160\t  description: 'Original vs double-rewrite (same style) pairwise comparison。 Quantifies\n161\t    original preference confound independent of style。 与 exp-022 共享 underlying test\n162\t    mechanism 但 framing 不同。\n163\t\n164\t    '\n165\t  expected_results:\n166\t    gpt4o:\n167\t      formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.558\n168\t      formality_bt_ci:\n169\t      - 0.488\n170\t      - 0.628\n171\t      formality_bt_p: 0.11\n172\t      verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.566\n173\t      verbosity_bt_ci:\n174\t      - 0.494\n175\t      - 0.638\n176\t      verbosity_bt_p: 0.07\n177\t    qwen32b:\n178\t      formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.551\n179\t      formality_bt_ci:\n180\t      - 0.481\n181\t      - 0.621\n182\t      formality_bt_p: 0.16\n183\t      verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.574\n184\t      verbosity_bt_ci:\n185\t      - 0.502\n186\t      - 0.646\n187\t      verbosity_bt_p: 0.05\n188\t    cross_judge_mean_original_pref: 0.562\n189\t    cross_judge_ci:\n190\t    - 0.51\n191\t    - 0.61\n192\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心预期：judges 对 original 有轻微系统偏好 (BT ~55-57%)， 但大部分 individual\n193\t    tests 不显著或 marginal (p=0.05-0.16)。方向 一致性 (4/4 cells prefer original) 暗示这是 genuine\n194\t    rewriting artifact 而非 noise。原因：rewriting 即使保持 style 不变也可能 引入微妙 fluency/coherence\n195\t    变化，judges 能部分检测到。这是 pairwise format 的 inherent limitation，与 Jeong et al. 2025\n196\t    Comparative Trap concern 一致。\n197\t\n198\t    关键：此 original preference (~6pp above 50%) 远小于 observed style BT (13-27pp above\n199\t    50%)。Net style effect 是 original preference 的 2-4 倍，证明 style bias 信号 dominates。\n200\t\n201\t    '\n202\t  tables:\n203\t  - Original preference BT by judge × axis, with observed style BT for comparison\n204\t  figures_description:\n205\t  - 'Paired bar: original preference BT vs observed style BT, showing gap = net style\n206\t    effect'\n207\t  analysis: '与 exp-022 结论一致。Original preference 是 real but bounded。 论文需要 explicit\n208\t    acknowledgment：\"pairwise format introduces a small rewriting-artifact bias (~6pp)\n209\t    that is bounded and small relative to the observed style signal (13-27pp).\"\n210\t\n211\t    '\n212\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\n213\t  plan_id: exp-009\n214\t  description: 'Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals。 与\n215\t    Qwen3-32B 和 GPT-4o rewriter 结果对比。Three independent rewriter families。\n216\t\n217\t    '\n218\t  expected_results:\n219\t    cf_generated: 100\n220\t    nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n221\t    nli_mean: 0.878\n222\t    bt_p_formal: 0.638\n223\t    bt_ci:\n224\t    - 0.555\n225\t    - 0.721\n226\t    bt_p: 0.003\n227\t    likert_ate: -0.06\n228\t    likert_p: 0.55\n229\t    blindspot: true\n230\t    vs_qwen_rewriter_bt: 0.665\n231\t    vs_qwen_delta_pp: -2.7\n232\t    vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n233\t    vs_gpt4o_delta_pp: -0.6\n234\t    all_ci_overlap: true\n235\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下第 3 个 rewriter 确认 rewriter-independence。Llama rewriter\n236\t    NLI pass rate 略低 (85% vs 88-90%)，反映不同 rewriting behavior，但 BT (63.8%) 落入 Qwen\n237\t    (66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (64.4%) 的 CI 内。三个独立 rewriter families (open-CN, proprietary-US,\n238\t    open-US) 产生 formality BT 63-67% range。Llama 的 rewriting 可能 更 aggressive (lower\n239\t    NLI pass)，但经 NLI gate 过滤后信号一致。\n240\t\n241\t    '\n242\t  tables:\n243\t  - '3-rewriter comparison: Qwen3-32B 66.5% [58.5,73.9], GPT-4o 64.4% [56.1,72.8],\n244\t    Llama-70B 63.8% [55.5,72.1] — all CIs overlap'\n245\t  figures_description:\n246\t  - 'Forest plot: BT P(formal) by rewriter with 95% CIs, showing mutual overlap around\n247\t    64-66%'\n248\t  analysis: 'Rewriter-independence now established with 3 families。Addresses concern\n249\t    that detected bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact。 Useful robustness but\n250\t    not a game-changer in median tier。\n251\t\n252\t    '\n253\t- name: Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\n254\t  plan_id: exp-021\n255\t  description: 'Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge。Pairwise + Likert on verbosity\n256\t    和 formality (LLMBar)。Reuses existing NLI-filtered pairs。Three architecture families:\n257\t    GPT-4o (proprietary), Qwen3-32B (open-CN), Llama-70B (open-US)。\n258\t\n259\t    '\n260\t  expected_results:\n261\t    verbosity:\n262\t      n_pairs: 86\n263\t      n_comparisons: 172\n264\t      consistency_rate: 0.58\n265\t      verbose_win_rate_consistent: 0.72\n266\t      bt_p_verbose: 0.66\n267\t      bt_ci:\n268\t      - 0.586\n269\t      - 0.734\n270\t      bt_p: 0.002\n271\t      sign_test_p: 0.008\n272\t      likert_ate: -0.082\n273\t      likert_p: 0.45\n274\t      likert_d: -0.075\n275\t      likert_tie_rate: 0.62\n276\t      gee_verbose_or: 5.21\n277\t      gee_verbose_ci:\n278\t      - 2.1\n279\t      - 12.92\n280\t      gee_verbose_p: 0.0004\n281\t      gee_orig_or: 0.72\n282\t      gee_orig_ci:\n283\t      - 0.3\n284\t      - 1.73\n285\t      gee_orig_p: 0.46\n286\t      blindspot_confirmed: true\n287\t    formality:\n288\t      n_pairs: 88\n289\t      n_comparisons: 176\n290\t      consistency_rate: 0.52\n291\t      formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.587\n292\t      bt_p_formal: 0.548\n293\t      bt_ci:\n294\t      - 0.476\n295\t      - 0.62\n296\t      bt_p: 0.18\n297\t      sign_test_p: 0.28\n298\t      likert_ate: 0.032\n299\t      likert_p: 0.72\n300\t      likert_d: 0.028\n301\t      likert_tie_rate: 0.69\n302\t      gee_formal_or: 1.35\n303\t      gee_formal_ci:\n304\t      - 0.7\n305\t      - 2.6\n306\t      gee_formal_p: 0.37\n307\t      gee_orig_or: 2.83\n308\t      gee_orig_ci:\n309\t      - 1.41\n310\t      - 5.68\n311\t      gee_orig_p: 0.003\n312\t      blindspot_confirmed: false\n313\t    cross_judge_summary:\n314\t      verbosity_biased: 3/3 — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3 77.3%, Llama 66.0%\n315\t      formality_biased: 2/3 — GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%; Llama 54.8% NS\n316\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档定义性实验。\n317\t\n318\t    Verbosity: Llama-70B 显示 significant bias (BT 66.0%, p=0.002)，但 effect 弱于 GPT-4o\n319\t    (76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE 确认纯 style 效应 (verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, originality\n320\t    OR=0.72 NS)。Pattern 与 其他两个 judge 一致——verbosity bias 是 confound-free 的。Llama 更弱\n321\t    可能因为 70B 参数量 vs GPT-4o/Qwen3 更大或更 instruction-tuned。 BT 66% 虽低于其他 judge 但仍显著且远超\n322\t    placebo baseline (~56%)。 Likert 照常 NS (p=0.45)，Blindspot 确认。\n323\t\n324\t    Formality: Llama-70B 仅 weak/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。CI [47.6%, 62.0%] 包含 50%。GEE\n325\t    显示 style OR=1.35 NS 但 originality OR=2.83 p=0.003 —— Llama 对 formality 不敏感但对 originality\n326\t    敏感。这与 GPT-4o/Qwen 不同（它们两者均显著）。原因：formality 本身是 \"conditional style effect\" (originality\n327\t    confound 强)，Llama 的 weaker instruction-following 能力使其不 pick up 较弱的 formality signal，但\n328\t    still sensitive 到 content quality (originality)。BT 54.8% 与 Claude (56.2%) 接近，\n329\t    但原因不同——Claude 是设计上 debiased，Llama 可能只是 less sensitive。\n330\t\n331\t    Impact: C1 必须改为 \"most tested judges\"。C2 分层：verbosity 3/3 robust, formality 2/3。SF3\n332\t    得 ~2.5/3 分 (verbosity full credit, formality half credit)。论文不能说 \"all LLM judges\n333\t    have formality bias\" 但可说 \"verbosity bias universal across tested architectures\"。\n334\t\n335\t    '\n336\t  tables:\n337\t  - Three-judge BT/Likert/GEE comparison for verbosity and formality\n338\t  - 'Cross-judge Blindspot matrix: 3 judges × 2 axes'\n339\t  figures_description:\n340\t  - 'Forest plot: BT by judge for verbosity (three sig) and formality (two sig, one\n341\t    NS)'\n342\t  - 'GEE coefficient plot: Style OR vs Originality OR per judge × axis, showing Llama\n343\t    formality divergence'\n344\t  analysis: 'Llama 结果强制 per-axis stratification。Verbosity 成为论文最强 claim (3/3 judges,\n345\t    confound-free, 7-method sensitivity confirmed)。 Formality 降级为 \"conditional effect\n346\t    detected by majority of judges\" with originality confound caveat。这不是 fatal——2/3\n347\t    judges 仍是 meaningful generalization，且 Llama formality 的 point estimate (54.8%)\n348\t    是 directionally correct，只是 underpowered。论文可加 power analysis 显示 n=88 pairs 对 Δ=5pp\n349\t    effect 只有 ~30% power。\n350\t\n351\t    '\n352\t- name: Double-rewrite placebo BT\n353\t  plan_id: exp-022\n354\t  description: 'MF1 最强防御。Original vs double-rewrite (same style, only rewriting artifact)。GPT-4o\n355\t    + Qwen3-32B judges × formality + verbosity axes。\n356\t\n357\t    '\n358\t  expected_results:\n359\t    gpt4o_formality_placebo:\n360\t      n_pairs: 88\n361\t      bt_prefer_original: 0.555\n362\t      bt_ci:\n363\t      - 0.485\n364\t      - 0.625\n365\t      bt_p: 0.12\n366\t    gpt4o_verbosity_placebo:\n367\t      n_pairs: 86\n368\t      bt_prefer_original: 0.563\n369\t      bt_ci:\n370\t      - 0.491\n371\t      - 0.635\n372\t      bt_p: 0.08\n373\t    qwen32b_formality_placebo:\n374\t      n_pairs: 88\n375\t      bt_prefer_original: 0.548\n376\t      bt_ci:\n377\t      - 0.478\n378\t      - 0.618\n379\t      bt_p: 0.17\n380\t    qwen32b_verbosity_placebo:\n381\t      n_pairs: 86\n382\t      bt_prefer_original: 0.571\n383\t      bt_ci:\n384\t      - 0.499\n385\t      - 0.643\n386\t      bt_p: 0.06\n387\t    amplification_bounds:\n388\t      formality_gpt4o:\n389\t        observed_bt: 0.63\n390\t        placebo_bt: 0.555\n391\t        net_style_effect_pp: 7.5\n392\t        amplification_fraction: 0.42\n393\t      formality_qwen32b:\n394\t        observed_bt: 0.665\n395\t        placebo_bt: 0.548\n396\t        net_style_effect_pp: 11.7\n397\t        amplification_fraction: 0.29\n398\t      verbosity_gpt4o:\n399\t        observed_bt: 0.76\n400\t        placebo_bt: 0.563\n401\t        net_style_effect_pp: 19.7\n402\t        amplification_fraction: 0.24\n403\t      verbosity_qwen32b:\n404\t        observed_bt: 0.773\n405\t        placebo_bt: 0.571\n406\t        net_style_effect_pp: 20.2\n407\t        amplification_fraction: 0.26\n408\t  result_rationale: \"Median 档核心。Placebo BT 不是干净的 50%，而是 54.8-57.1%，略高。 这意味着 pairwise\\\n409\t    \\ format 对 rewrites 有轻微系统偏好——rewriting artifact 贡献了 ~5-7pp bias component。但 individual\\\n410\t    \\ cell tests 大多不显著 (p=0.06-0.17)，方向一致 (4/4 prefer original)。\\nAmplification bound\\\n411\t    \\ 计算： - Verbosity: observed 76-77% − placebo 56-57% = net ~20pp。\\n  Amplification\\\n412\t    \\ fraction 24-26%——rewriting noise 至多解释 1/4\\n  observed signal。\\n- Formality:\\\n413\t    \\ observed 63-67% − placebo 55-56% = net ~8-12pp。\\n  Amplification fraction 29-42%——formality\\\n414\t    \\ 轴 amplification\\n  component 较大，因为 observed effect 本身较弱。\\n\\nVerbosity 的 net\\\n415\t    \\ style effect 是 robust 的 (20pp, ~3-4× placebo)。 Formality 的 net style effect\\\n416\t    \\ 更 marginal (8-12pp, ~1.5-2× placebo)， reviewer 可合理 challenge。\\n论文叙事从 \\\"pairwise\\\n417\t    \\ doesn't amplify\\\" 改为 \\\"pairwise amplifies at most ~5-7pp, bounded and small\\\n418\t    \\ relative to verbosity signal (20pp), moderate relative to formality signal (8-12pp).\\\"\\\n419\t    \\ 需要新增 Amplification Bound 小节。\\n\"\n420\t  tables:\n421\t  - Placebo BT by judge × axis with observed BT and net style effect\n422\t  - 'Amplification fraction calculation: (placebo−0.50)/(observed−0.50)'\n423\t  figures_description:\n424\t  - 'Stacked bar: observed BT decomposed into placebo component (gray) + net style\n425\t    effect (blue) per axis'\n426\t  - 'Forest plot: placebo BT across 4 cells with 95% CIs, dashed line at 50%'\n427\t  analysis: 'MF1 defense 从 \"eliminated\" 降级为 \"bounded\"。Verbosity 稳健 (amplification\n428\t    fraction ~25%)，formality 更脆弱 (up to 42%)。 论文需要 honest acknowledgment。Positive\n429\t    spin: explicit bounding demonstrates methodological rigor, which ACL reviewers\n430\t    value。 Negative: reviewer 可 argue formality claim 的 nearly half 可能是 amplification\n431\t    artifact。Mitigation: 配合 GEE decomposition (style OR 仍然 significant after controlling\n432\t    originality) 和 Claude negative control (same format, no bias)，multi-layered defense\n433\t    虽非 definitive 但 sufficient for Findings。\n434\t\n435\t    '\n436\t- name: NLI gate ablation\n437\t  plan_id: exp-023\n438\t  description: 'BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs for verbosity 和 formality。\n439\t    Quantify NLI gate contribution to BT signal。\n440\t\n441\t    '\n442\t  expected_results:\n443\t    formality:\n444\t      nli_pass:\n445\t        n: 88\n446\t        bt: 0.665\n447\t        ci:\n448\t        - 0.585\n449\t        - 0.739\n450\t        p: 0.0001\n451\t      nli_fail:\n452\t        n: 12\n453\t        bt: 0.618\n454\t        ci:\n455\t        - 0.378\n456\t        - 0.858\n457\t        p: 0.38\n458\t      all_pairs:\n459\t        n: 100\n460\t        bt: 0.609\n461\t        ci:\n462\t        - 0.538\n463\t        - 0.678\n464\t        p: 0.001\n465\t      pass_minus_fail_pp: 4.7\n466\t      pass_minus_fail_ci:\n467\t      - -20.2\n468\t      - 29.6\n469\t      difference_significant: false\n470\t    verbosity:\n471\t      nli_pass:\n472\t        n: 86\n473\t        bt: 0.773\n474\t        ci:\n475\t        - 0.703\n476\t        - 0.843\n477\t        p: 0.0001\n478\t      nli_fail:\n479\t        n: 14\n480\t        bt: 0.738\n481\t        ci:\n482\t        - 0.523\n483\t        - 0.953\n484\t        p: 0.04\n485\t      all_pairs:\n486\t        n: 100\n487\t        bt: 0.733\n488\t        ci:\n489\t        - 0.66\n490\t        - 0.8\n491\t        p: 0.0001\n492\t      pass_minus_fail_pp: 3.5\n493\t      pass_minus_fail_ci:\n494\t      - -18.8\n495\t      - 25.8\n496\t      difference_significant: false\n497\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档：NLI ablation 方向正确但 inconclusive。NLI-pass BT 略高于 NLI-fail\n498\t    (formality +4.7pp, verbosity +3.5pp)，落在 tier 定义的 [-3, 8]pp 范围内。但 NLI-fail n 极小\n499\t    (12-14 pairs)，CI 宽达 ±20-25pp，差异远不显著。\n500\t\n501\t    方向性解读：NLI gate 过滤了一些 content-mediated comparisons (fail pairs BT 略低，可能因 content\n502\t    changes dilute style signal)。但 small n 使这只能作为 \"bounding evidence\"。\n503\t\n504\t    All-pairs BT 仍然显著 (formality 60.9%, verbosity 73.3%)——即使不用 NLI gate style bias\n505\t    仍存在。这是 double-edged：(1) bias 是 robust finding 不依赖 NLI gate；(2) reviewer 可能问 \"if\n506\t    bias exists without NLI, why is NLI gate needed?\" 答案：NLI gate 提高 causal credibility\n507\t    (content control)，不是 detection 的必要条件。All-pairs BT 略低于 NLI-pass BT 说明 content contamination\n508\t    dilutes signal ~4pp，NLI gate cleans this up。\n509\t\n510\t    '\n511\t  tables:\n512\t  - BT by NLI status (pass/fail/all) × axis with CIs\n513\t  figures_description:\n514\t  - 'Point-range plot: BT by NLI status, showing wide CI on fail group vs narrow CI\n515\t    on pass group'\n516\t  analysis: 'NLI ablation 不提供 strong evidence。Directional consistency 是 suggestive\n517\t    但 not conclusive。论文应报告为 bounding analysis acknowledging n limitation。Key framing:\n518\t    \"NLI gate improves internal validity but finding is robust to gating decisions.\"\n519\t    这实际上是 robustness positive。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t- name: Cross-axis gradient formalization\n523\t  plan_id: exp-024\n524\t  description: 'NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT across\n525\t    3 axes。Qualitative anti-amplification argument。\n526\t\n527\t    '\n528\t  expected_results:\n529\t    gradient:\n530\t      register:\n531\t        nli_reject_rate: 0.06\n532\t        bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.553\n533\t      formality:\n534\t        nli_reject_rate: 0.112\n535\t        bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.647\n536\t      verbosity:\n537\t        nli_reject_rate: 0.14\n538\t        bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.77\n539\t    spearman_r: 1.0\n540\t    spearman_p: 0.333\n541\t    n_points: 3\n542\t    monotonic: true\n543\t    interpretation_ambiguous: true\n544\t  result_rationale: \"Median 档：3 data points 显示 perfect rank correlation (register\\\n545\t    \\ < formality < verbosity on both NLI reject 和 BT)。Spearman r=1.0 但 n=3 给出 p=0.333——统计上\\\n546\t    \\ meaningless。\\n更关键的是方向性 ambiguity： - Amplification 解释：rewriting 越 invasive (higher\\\n547\t    \\ NLI reject) →\\n  更多 format artifact → higher BT。Verbosity rewriting 最 invasive\\n\\\n548\t    \\  (14% reject)，BT 最高 (77%)。\\n- Detection 解释：真实 bias 最强的 axis (verbosity) 恰好需要最\\n\\\n549\t    \\  invasive rewriting 来改变 style。BT 反映 true bias 不同，不是\\n  amplification 不同。\\n\\n\\\n550\t    两个 hypothesis 都能解释 observed pattern。3 points 无法区分。 这使 cross-axis gradient 成为 paper\\\n551\t    \\ 最弱的 anti-amplification argument——qualitative at best，可能被 reviewer 直接 dismiss。\\n\"\n552\t  tables:\n553\t  - 'Three-axis gradient: NLI reject rate, mean BT, Spearman r=1.0 p=0.333'\n554\t  figures_description:\n555\t  - 'Scatter: NLI rejection rate (x) vs mean BT (y) for 3 axes with labels, Spearman\n556\t    annotation'\n557\t  analysis: Cross-axis gradient 在 median 档是 paper 最弱 argument。只有 3 points，统计无意义，方向\n558\t    ambiguous。应放入 supplementary 或 降为一句话 mention，不作为 main defense。Main anti-amplification\n559\t    defense 应依靠 exp-022 placebo BT (explicit amplification bound) + Claude negative\n560\t    control + NLI gate。Cross-axis gradient 至多 提供 \"observation consistent with per-axis\n561\t    variation\" 的 qualitative color。\n562\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b418a75-678d-4fa3-85ef-47aa6f4921e4","uuid":"836c6880-3535-4d4d-880c-237c9c70d5d6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:17:05.796Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Claims require axis-stratification and bounded-amplification\n  qualifier. C2 Blindspot stratified: verbosity = robust 3/3 cross-judge finding,\n  formality = 2/3 judges (Llama weak/NS). C1 reworded to \"CSD detects per-axis style\n  bias in most tested judges.\" Comparative Trap defense downgraded from \"eliminated\"\n  to \"bounded\": placebo BT 54-57% means rewriting artifact contributes ~5-7pp, but\n  observed BT 63-77% far exceeds placebo → style bias signal real, bounded amplification\n  acknowledged. Paper adds explicit amplification_bound = observed_BT − placebo_BT\n  = net_style_effect. SF3 partially addressed (2.5/3 judges). MF1 bounded not eliminated.\n  Score 3.5-3.75, strong Findings case, marginal Main.\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 'Formality pairwise with Gemini-2.0-Flash as 4th judge. Claude already\n    done (negative control). Reuses existing 100 formality counterfactual pairs with\n    NLI≥0.90 filtering.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gemini_n_pairs: 88\n    gemini_consistency_rate: 0.57\n    gemini_formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.66\n    gemini_bt_p_formal: 0.615\n    gemini_bt_ci:\n    - 0.541\n    - 0.689\n    gemini_bt_p: 0.004\n    gemini_likert_ate: -0.045\n    gemini_likert_p: 0.68\n    gemini_likert_d: -0.038\n    gemini_gee_style_or: 2.45\n    gemini_gee_style_p: 0.012\n    gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.28\n    gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.003\n    gemini_blindspot: true\n  result_rationale: 'Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 mid-tier proprietary model，在 median 档下展示 中等\n    formality bias (BT 61.5%)，弱于 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 但与 GPT-4o (63.0%) 相近。GEE 显示 style\n    和 originality 双重效应均显著—— formality 在此 judge 也是\"conditional style effect\"。Likert\n    NS (p=0.68) 确认 Blindspot。加了第 4 个 biased judge 但不改变故事结构， 4/5 judges show formality\n    bias，Claude 仍为唯一 negative control。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Cross-judge formality BT: GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%, Gemini 61.5%, Llama 54.8%(NS),\n    Claude 56.2%(NS) — all on LLMBar n≈88'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CIs, three clustered 61-67%,\n    two near 50%'\n  analysis: '增加一个 data point 但不解锁 qualitative upgrade。Paper 可报告 3/5 judges biased\n    on formality (如果 Llama NS 不算)。对 generalizability 有帮助但 marginal。exp-001 不是 Round\n    5 核心实验。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark formality (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench × additional judges)\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 'Formality pairwise on AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench with Qwen3-32B 和 Claude\n    as judges. GPT-4o 已 done (AlpacaEval BT 72.7%, MT-Bench BT 69.2%). 需要新 counterfactual\n    generation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality:\n      n_pairs: 86\n      bt_p_formal: 0.684\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.607\n      - 0.755\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: 0.095\n      likert_p: 0.31\n      blindspot: true\n    qwen32b_mtbench_formality:\n      n_pairs: 73\n      bt_p_formal: 0.712\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.635\n      - 0.782\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: 0.19\n      likert_p: 0.022\n      likert_d: 0.185\n      blindspot: false\n    claude_alpacaeval_formality:\n      n_pairs: 86\n      bt_p_formal: 0.538\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.463\n      - 0.613\n      bt_p: 0.29\n      blindspot: false\n    claude_mtbench_formality:\n      n_pairs: 73\n      bt_p_formal: 0.527\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.448\n      - 0.606\n      bt_p: 0.42\n      blindspot: false\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 cross-benchmark replication 大部分一致。Qwen3-32B 在 AlpacaEval\n    (BT 68.4%) 和 MT-Bench (71.2%) 上均显示 formality bias， 与 LLMBar (66.5%) 一致。MT-Bench\n    的 Qwen Likert marginally sig (p=0.022, d=0.185)——此 cell 不是 Blindspot，类似 GPT-4o\n    MT-Bench pattern。原因：MT-Bench items 更长更复杂，style 差异在 absolute scoring 中更 salient，Likert\n    部分检测到。Claude 在两个 benchmark 均 NS，negative control 跨 benchmark generalize。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - '3×3 Benchmark × Judge formality BT matrix: 6/9 cells Blindspot, 2/9 both-sig\n    (MT-Bench GPT-4o+Qwen), 1/9 neither (Claude always NS)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: BT P(formal) across judge × benchmark, Blindspot cells shaded'\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark replication 揭示 Blindspot 的 boundary condition： 只有 BT\n    > ~70% 且 item complexity 较高时 Likert 才开始 detect。这 与 attenuation spectrum narrative\n    一致——BT 60-70% 区间是 Likert 完全 attenuation zone。MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert partially detects\n    的 benchmark，因为 formality BT 在此 benchmark 最强 (69-71%)。\n\n    '\n- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 'Systematic comparison of Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT across all judge\n    × benchmark × axis cells. Formal quantification of Blindspot phenomenon boundaries.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_cells_evaluated: 18\n    blindspot_cells: 10\n    both_sig_cells: 3\n    neither_sig_cells: 5\n    blindspot_by_axis:\n      verbosity: 5/6 cells Blindspot\n      formality: 4/6 cells Blindspot\n      register: 1/6 cells Blindspot\n    attenuation_spectrum:\n      bt_55_to_67_pct: complete Likert attenuation (all p>0.15)\n      bt_68_to_77_pct: near-complete attenuation (5/6 Likert NS, 1/6 p=0.022)\n      bt_above_80_pct: partial detection (AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen d=0.375 p=0.0003)\n    likert_detection_threshold_bt: 0.8\n  result_rationale: '在 median 档下，sensitivity analysis 覆盖 18 cells (3 axes × 3 benchmarks\n    × 2+ judges)。Blindspot 是 dominant pattern (10/18 cells)， 但不 universal。Both-sig\n    cells 集中在 BT > 80% 的 extreme effects (AlpacaEval verbosity) 和 MT-Bench (高 item\n    complexity)。Neither-sig cells 均为 Claude (negative control) 和 Llama formality (真实无\n    bias)。 Attenuation spectrum 在 BT ~80% 处有清晰 threshold——低于此值 Likert 完全 fail，高于此值开始部分\n    detect。这支持 \"measurement attenuation\" interpretation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Full 18-cell matrix: Judge × Benchmark × Axis with BT, Likert p, d, Blindspot\n    Y/N'\n  - 'Attenuation spectrum: BT range → Likert detection rate'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: BT (x) vs Likert |d| (y) across 18 cells, horizontal line at d=0.2 threshold,\n    vertical line at BT=80%'\n  analysis: 'Sensitivity analysis 是 C2 最强 evidence 之一。Attenuation spectrum 是 consistent\n    and replicable，不是单 cell fluke。BT ~80% threshold 意味着大多数 real-world style biases\n    (likely 55-75%) 会被 standard Likert evaluation 漏掉。Practical implication 明确。\n\n    '\n- name: RATE double-rewrite control (original preference quantification)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Original vs double-rewrite (same style) pairwise comparison。 Quantifies\n    original preference confound independent of style。 与 exp-022 共享 underlying test\n    mechanism 但 framing 不同。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o:\n      formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.558\n      formality_bt_ci:\n      - 0.488\n      - 0.628\n      formality_bt_p: 0.11\n      verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.566\n      verbosity_bt_ci:\n      - 0.494\n      - 0.638\n      verbosity_bt_p: 0.07\n    qwen32b:\n      formality_bt_prefer_original: 0.551\n      formality_bt_ci:\n      - 0.481\n      - 0.621\n      formality_bt_p: 0.16\n      verbosity_bt_prefer_original: 0.574\n      verbosity_bt_ci:\n      - 0.502\n      - 0.646\n      verbosity_bt_p: 0.05\n    cross_judge_mean_original_pref: 0.562\n    cross_judge_ci:\n    - 0.51\n    - 0.61\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心预期：judges 对 original 有轻微系统偏好 (BT ~55-57%)， 但大部分 individual\n    tests 不显著或 marginal (p=0.05-0.16)。方向 一致性 (4/4 cells prefer original) 暗示这是 genuine\n    rewriting artifact 而非 noise。原因：rewriting 即使保持 style 不变也可能 引入微妙 fluency/coherence\n    变化，judges 能部分检测到。这是 pairwise format 的 inherent limitation，与 Jeong et al. 2025\n    Comparative Trap concern 一致。\n\n    关键：此 original preference (~6pp above 50%) 远小于 observed style BT (13-27pp above\n    50%)。Net style effect 是 original preference 的 2-4 倍，证明 style bias 信号 dominates。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - Original preference BT by judge × axis, with observed style BT for comparison\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar: original preference BT vs observed style BT, showing gap = net style\n    effect'\n  analysis: '与 exp-022 结论一致。Original preference 是 real but bounded。 论文需要 explicit\n    acknowledgment：\"pairwise format introduces a small rewriting-artifact bias (~6pp)\n    that is bounded and small relative to the observed style signal (13-27pp).\"\n\n    '\n- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals。 与\n    Qwen3-32B 和 GPT-4o rewriter 结果对比。Three independent rewriter families。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cf_generated: 100\n    nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n    nli_mean: 0.878\n    bt_p_formal: 0.638\n    bt_ci:\n    - 0.555\n    - 0.721\n    bt_p: 0.003\n    likert_ate: -0.06\n    likert_p: 0.55\n    blindspot: true\n    vs_qwen_rewriter_bt: 0.665\n    vs_qwen_delta_pp: -2.7\n    vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n    vs_gpt4o_delta_pp: -0.6\n    all_ci_overlap: true\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下第 3 个 rewriter 确认 rewriter-independence。Llama rewriter\n    NLI pass rate 略低 (85% vs 88-90%)，反映不同 rewriting behavior，但 BT (63.8%) 落入 Qwen\n    (66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (64.4%) 的 CI 内。三个独立 rewriter families (open-CN, proprietary-US,\n    open-US) 产生 formality BT 63-67% range。Llama 的 rewriting 可能 更 aggressive (lower\n    NLI pass)，但经 NLI gate 过滤后信号一致。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - '3-rewriter comparison: Qwen3-32B 66.5% [58.5,73.9], GPT-4o 64.4% [56.1,72.8],\n    Llama-70B 63.8% [55.5,72.1] — all CIs overlap'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: BT P(formal) by rewriter with 95% CIs, showing mutual overlap around\n    64-66%'\n  analysis: 'Rewriter-independence now established with 3 families。Addresses concern\n    that detected bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact。 Useful robustness but\n    not a game-changer in median tier。\n\n    '\n- name: Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\n  plan_id: exp-021\n  description: 'Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge。Pairwise + Likert on verbosity\n    和 formality (LLMBar)。Reuses existing NLI-filtered pairs。Three architecture families:\n    GPT-4o (proprietary), Qwen3-32B (open-CN), Llama-70B (open-US)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    verbosity:\n      n_pairs: 86\n      n_comparisons: 172\n      consistency_rate: 0.58\n      verbose_win_rate_consistent: 0.72\n      bt_p_verbose: 0.66\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.586\n      - 0.734\n      bt_p: 0.002\n      sign_test_p: 0.008\n      likert_ate: -0.082\n      likert_p: 0.45\n      likert_d: -0.075\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.62\n      gee_verbose_or: 5.21\n      gee_verbose_ci:\n      - 2.1\n      - 12.92\n      gee_verbose_p: 0.0004\n      gee_orig_or: 0.72\n      gee_orig_ci:\n      - 0.3\n      - 1.73\n      gee_orig_p: 0.46\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    formality:\n      n_pairs: 88\n      n_comparisons: 176\n      consistency_rate: 0.52\n      formal_win_rate_consistent: 0.587\n      bt_p_formal: 0.548\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.476\n      - 0.62\n      bt_p: 0.18\n      sign_test_p: 0.28\n      likert_ate: 0.032\n      likert_p: 0.72\n      likert_d: 0.028\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.69\n      gee_formal_or: 1.35\n      gee_formal_ci:\n      - 0.7\n      - 2.6\n      gee_formal_p: 0.37\n      gee_orig_or: 2.83\n      gee_orig_ci:\n      - 1.41\n      - 5.68\n      gee_orig_p: 0.003\n      blindspot_confirmed: false\n    cross_judge_summary:\n      verbosity_biased: 3/3 — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3 77.3%, Llama 66.0%\n      formality_biased: 2/3 — GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%; Llama 54.8% NS\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档定义性实验。\n\n    Verbosity: Llama-70B 显示 significant bias (BT 66.0%, p=0.002)，但 effect 弱于 GPT-4o\n    (76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE 确认纯 style 效应 (verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, originality\n    OR=0.72 NS)。Pattern 与 其他两个 judge 一致——verbosity bias 是 confound-free 的。Llama 更弱\n    可能因为 70B 参数量 vs GPT-4o/Qwen3 更大或更 instruction-tuned。 BT 66% 虽低于其他 judge 但仍显著且远超\n    placebo baseline (~56%)。 Likert 照常 NS (p=0.45)，Blindspot 确认。\n\n    Formality: Llama-70B 仅 weak/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。CI [47.6%, 62.0%] 包含 50%。GEE\n    显示 style OR=1.35 NS 但 originality OR=2.83 p=0.003 —— Llama 对 formality 不敏感但对 originality\n    敏感。这与 GPT-4o/Qwen 不同（它们两者均显著）。原因：formality 本身是 \"conditional style effect\" (originality\n    confound 强)，Llama 的 weaker instruction-following 能力使其不 pick up 较弱的 formality signal，但\n    still sensitive 到 content quality (originality)。BT 54.8% 与 Claude (56.2%) 接近，\n    但原因不同——Claude 是设计上 debiased，Llama 可能只是 less sensitive。\n\n    Impact: C1 必须改为 \"most tested judges\"。C2 分层：verbosity 3/3 robust, formality 2/3。SF3\n    得 ~2.5/3 分 (verbosity full credit, formality half credit)。论文不能说 \"all LLM judges\n    have formality bias\" 但可说 \"verbosity bias universal across tested architectures\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - Three-judge BT/Likert/GEE comparison for verbosity and formality\n  - 'Cross-judge Blindspot matrix: 3 judges × 2 axes'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: BT by judge for verbosity (three sig) and formality (two sig, one\n    NS)'\n  - 'GEE coefficient plot: Style OR vs Originality OR per judge × axis, showing Llama\n    formality divergence'\n  analysis: 'Llama 结果强制 per-axis stratification。Verbosity 成为论文最强 claim (3/3 judges,\n    confound-free, 7-method sensitivity confirmed)。 Formality 降级为 \"conditional effect\n    detected by majority of judges\" with originality confound caveat。这不是 fatal——2/3\n    judges 仍是 meaningful generalization，且 Llama formality 的 point estimate (54.8%)\n    是 directionally correct，只是 underpowered。论文可加 power analysis 显示 n=88 pairs 对 Δ=5pp\n    effect 只有 ~30% power。\n\n    '\n- name: Double-rewrite placebo BT\n  plan_id: exp-022\n  description: 'MF1 最强防御。Original vs double-rewrite (same style, only rewriting artifact)。GPT-4o\n    + Qwen3-32B judges × formality + verbosity axes。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_formality_placebo:\n      n_pairs: 88\n      bt_prefer_original: 0.555\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.485\n      - 0.625\n      bt_p: 0.12\n    gpt4o_verbosity_placebo:\n      n_pairs: 86\n      bt_prefer_original: 0.563\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.491\n      - 0.635\n      bt_p: 0.08\n    qwen32b_formality_placebo:\n      n_pairs: 88\n      bt_prefer_original: 0.548\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.478\n      - 0.618\n      bt_p: 0.17\n    qwen32b_verbosity_placebo:\n      n_pairs: 86\n      bt_prefer_original: 0.571\n      bt_ci:\n      - 0.499\n      - 0.643\n      bt_p: 0.06\n    amplification_bounds:\n      formality_gpt4o:\n        observed_bt: 0.63\n        placebo_bt: 0.555\n        net_style_effect_pp: 7.5\n        amplification_fraction: 0.42\n      formality_qwen32b:\n        observed_bt: 0.665\n        placebo_bt: 0.548\n        net_style_effect_pp: 11.7\n        amplification_fraction: 0.29\n      verbosity_gpt4o:\n        observed_bt: 0.76\n        placebo_bt: 0.563\n        net_style_effect_pp: 19.7\n        amplification_fraction: 0.24\n      verbosity_qwen32b:\n        observed_bt: 0.773\n        placebo_bt: 0.571\n        net_style_effect_pp: 20.2\n        amplification_fraction: 0.26\n  result_rationale: \"Median 档核心。Placebo BT 不是干净的 50%，而是 54.8-57.1%，略高。 这意味着 pairwise\\\n    \\ format 对 rewrites 有轻微系统偏好——rewriting artifact 贡献了 ~5-7pp bias component。但 individual\\\n    \\ cell tests 大多不显著 (p=0.06-0.17)，方向一致 (4/4 prefer original)。\\nAmplification bound\\\n    \\ 计算： - Verbosity: observed 76-77% − placebo 56-57% = net ~20pp。\\n  Amplification\\\n    \\ fraction 24-26%——rewriting noise 至多解释 1/4\\n  observed signal。\\n- Formality:\\\n    \\ observed 63-67% − placebo 55-56% = net ~8-12pp。\\n  Amplification fraction 29-42%——formality\\\n    \\ 轴 amplification\\n  component 较大，因为 observed effect 本身较弱。\\n\\nVerbosity 的 net\\\n    \\ style effect 是 robust 的 (20pp, ~3-4× placebo)。 Formality 的 net style effect\\\n    \\ 更 marginal (8-12pp, ~1.5-2× placebo)， reviewer 可合理 challenge。\\n论文叙事从 \\\"pairwise\\\n    \\ doesn't amplify\\\" 改为 \\\"pairwise amplifies at most ~5-7pp, bounded and small\\\n    \\ relative to verbosity signal (20pp), moderate relative to formality signal (8-12pp).\\\"\\\n    \\ 需要新增 Amplification Bound 小节。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - Placebo BT by judge × axis with observed BT and net style effect\n  - 'Amplification fraction calculation: (placebo−0.50)/(observed−0.50)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar: observed BT decomposed into placebo component (gray) + net style\n    effect (blue) per axis'\n  - 'Forest plot: placebo BT across 4 cells with 95% CIs, dashed line at 50%'\n  analysis: 'MF1 defense 从 \"eliminated\" 降级为 \"bounded\"。Verbosity 稳健 (amplification\n    fraction ~25%)，formality 更脆弱 (up to 42%)。 论文需要 honest acknowledgment。Positive\n    spin: explicit bounding demonstrates methodological rigor, which ACL reviewers\n    value。 Negative: reviewer 可 argue formality claim 的 nearly half 可能是 amplification\n    artifact。Mitigation: 配合 GEE decomposition (style OR 仍然 significant after controlling\n    originality) 和 Claude negative control (same format, no bias)，multi-layered defense\n    虽非 definitive 但 sufficient for Findings。\n\n    '\n- name: NLI gate ablation\n  plan_id: exp-023\n  description: 'BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs for verbosity 和 formality。\n    Quantify NLI gate contribution to BT signal。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    formality:\n      nli_pass:\n        n: 88\n        bt: 0.665\n        ci:\n        - 0.585\n        - 0.739\n        p: 0.0001\n      nli_fail:\n        n: 12\n        bt: 0.618\n        ci:\n        - 0.378\n        - 0.858\n        p: 0.38\n      all_pairs:\n        n: 100\n        bt: 0.609\n        ci:\n        - 0.538\n        - 0.678\n        p: 0.001\n      pass_minus_fail_pp: 4.7\n      pass_minus_fail_ci:\n      - -20.2\n      - 29.6\n      difference_significant: false\n    verbosity:\n      nli_pass:\n        n: 86\n        bt: 0.773\n        ci:\n        - 0.703\n        - 0.843\n        p: 0.0001\n      nli_fail:\n        n: 14\n        bt: 0.738\n        ci:\n        - 0.523\n        - 0.953\n        p: 0.04\n      all_pairs:\n        n: 100\n        bt: 0.733\n        ci:\n        - 0.66\n        - 0.8\n        p: 0.0001\n      pass_minus_fail_pp: 3.5\n      pass_minus_fail_ci:\n      - -18.8\n      - 25.8\n      difference_significant: false\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档：NLI ablation 方向正确但 inconclusive。NLI-pass BT 略高于 NLI-fail\n    (formality +4.7pp, verbosity +3.5pp)，落在 tier 定义的 [-3, 8]pp 范围内。但 NLI-fail n 极小\n    (12-14 pairs)，CI 宽达 ±20-25pp，差异远不显著。\n\n    方向性解读：NLI gate 过滤了一些 content-mediated comparisons (fail pairs BT 略低，可能因 content\n    changes dilute style signal)。但 small n 使这只能作为 \"bounding evidence\"。\n\n    All-pairs BT 仍然显著 (formality 60.9%, verbosity 73.3%)——即使不用 NLI gate style bias\n    仍存在。这是 double-edged：(1) bias 是 robust finding 不依赖 NLI gate；(2) reviewer 可能问 \"if\n    bias exists without NLI, why is NLI gate needed?\" 答案：NLI gate 提高 causal credibility\n    (content control)，不是 detection 的必要条件。All-pairs BT 略低于 NLI-pass BT 说明 content contamination\n    dilutes signal ~4pp，NLI gate cleans this up。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - BT by NLI status (pass/fail/all) × axis with CIs\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Point-range plot: BT by NLI status, showing wide CI on fail group vs narrow CI\n    on pass group'\n  analysis: 'NLI ablation 不提供 strong evidence。Directional consistency 是 suggestive\n    但 not conclusive。论文应报告为 bounding analysis acknowledging n limitation。Key framing:\n    \"NLI gate improves internal validity but finding is robust to gating decisions.\"\n    这实际上是 robustness positive。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-axis gradient formalization\n  plan_id: exp-024\n  description: 'NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT across\n    3 axes。Qualitative anti-amplification argument。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gradient:\n      register:\n        nli_reject_rate: 0.06\n        bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.553\n      formality:\n        nli_reject_rate: 0.112\n        bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.647\n      verbosity:\n        nli_reject_rate: 0.14\n        bt_mean_across_2judges: 0.77\n    spearman_r: 1.0\n    spearman_p: 0.333\n    n_points: 3\n    monotonic: true\n    interpretation_ambiguous: true\n  result_rationale: \"Median 档：3 data points 显示 perfect rank correlation (register\\\n    \\ < formality < verbosity on both NLI reject 和 BT)。Spearman r=1.0 但 n=3 给出 p=0.333——统计上\\\n    \\ meaningless。\\n更关键的是方向性 ambiguity： - Amplification 解释：rewriting 越 invasive (higher\\\n    \\ NLI reject) →\\n  更多 format artifact → higher BT。Verbosity rewriting 最 invasive\\n\\\n    \\  (14% reject)，BT 最高 (77%)。\\n- Detection 解释：真实 bias 最强的 axis (verbosity) 恰好需要最\\n\\\n    \\  invasive rewriting 来改变 style。BT 反映 true bias 不同，不是\\n  amplification 不同。\\n\\n\\\n    两个 hypothesis 都能解释 observed pattern。3 points 无法区分。 这使 cross-axis gradient 成为 paper\\\n    \\ 最弱的 anti-amplification argument——qualitative at best，可能被 reviewer 直接 dismiss。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Three-axis gradient: NLI reject rate, mean BT, Spearman r=1.0 p=0.333'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: NLI rejection rate (x) vs mean BT (y) for 3 axes with labels, Spearman\n    annotation'\n  analysis: Cross-axis gradient 在 median 档是 paper 最弱 argument。只有 3 points，统计无意义，方向\n    ambiguous。应放入 supplementary 或 降为一句话 mention，不作为 main defense。Main anti-amplification\n    defense 应依靠 exp-022 placebo BT (explicit amplification bound) + Claude negative\n    control + NLI gate。Cross-axis gradient 至多 提供 \"observation consistent with per-axis\n    variation\" 的 qualitative color。\n","numLines":562,"startLine":1,"totalLines":562}}}
