ounds.\n\n### Results\n**Table 1 (LLMBar main results):**\n- Verbosity: GPT-4o BT=76.0% (p<.001), Qwen3=77.3% (p<.001), Llama=66.0% (p=.002). All Likert NS. Claude=54.1% NS (negative control). 3/3 Blindspot.\n- Formality: GPT-4o=63.0% (p<.001), Qwen3=66.5% (p<.001), Gemini=61.5% (p=.004), Llama=54.8% (p=.18 NS), Claude=56.2% NS. 3/4 Blindspot (excl Llama).\n\n**Table 2 (Cross-benchmark formality BT):**\n- Formality replicates across LLMBar/AlpacaEval/MT-Bench for GPT-4o (63-72.7%) and Qwen3 (66.5-71.2%). Claude NS everywhere. 5/6 cells Blindspot; MT-Bench Qwen3 Likert p=.022 is exception.\n\n**Table 3 (GEE decomposition):**\n- Verbosity: style ORs 5.21-13.10 (all p<.001), originality ORs all NS → pure style effect\n- Formality: both style and originality ORs significant for GPT-4o/Qwen3/Gemini; Llama only originality sig → conditional effect\n- Register: style ORs marginal, originality ORs dominant\n\n**Table 4 (Attenuation spectrum):**\n- BT 55-67%: 0/8 Likert detection\n- BT 68-77%: 1/6 Likert detection (17%)\n- BT >80%: 1/1 Likert detection (100%)\n\n**Table 5 (Amplification bounds):**\n- Placebo BT 54.8-57.1% (~5-7pp above 50%)\n- Verbosity net effect ~20pp, amplification fraction 24-26%\n- Formality net effect 7.5-11.7pp, amplification fraction 29-42%\n\n**Table 6 (Robustness):**\n- Rewriter independence: 3 rewriters produce BT 63.8-66.5% with overlapping CIs\n- NLI ablation: NLI-pass BT slightly higher but difference NS (small NLI-fail n=12-14)\n\n**Discussion mentions:** prompt-level debiasing is insufficient (tested \"style-blind\" prompts, Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp negligible).\n\n### Imagined experiments from review context (check coverage):\n- exp-001 (Gemini formality): ✓ covered in Table 1\n- exp-002 (cross-benchmark formality): ✓ covered in Table 2\n- exp-003 (sensitivity analysis): ✓ covered in Table 4\n- exp-005 (double-rewrite control): ✓ covered in Table 5\n- exp-009 (Llama rewriter): ✓ covered in Table 6\n- exp-021 (Llama judge): ✓ covered in Table 1\n- exp-022 (placebo BT): ✓ covered in Table 5\n- exp-023 (NLI ablation): ✓ covered in Table 6\n- exp-024 (cross-axis gradient): ✓ covered in Section 5.6\n\nAll imagined experiments are covered in the paper.\n\n### Your task\nWrite a detailed R1 review focusing on:\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the CSD pipeline well-designed? Are the statistical methods (BT, GEE, bootstrap) appropriate? Any methodological flaws?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Are controls adequate? Is the sample size sufficient? Are claims well-supported by evidence?\n3. **Specific concerns**: Amplification confound (especially formality at 42%), NLI gate design choices, BT threshold claim (only 1 cell >80%), GEE model specification.\n4. **Reproducibility**: Can this be replicated? Are enough details provided?\n\nOutput format — produce a structured review:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted, specific)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, specific, with severity: major/minor)\n- Questions for authors\n- Scores: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5), Overall Assessment (1-5, half-step)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Calibrate to EMNLP 2026 standards (~21% Main acceptance)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LygPnDBjmQXz9UNmYayUzR","session_id":"9b418a75-678d-4fa3-85ef-47aa6f4921e4","uuid":"15583220-1aeb-4ca3-baed-4edaf81a0a8f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:18:05.973Z"}
